  {
   "title": "Dijkstra in code",
   "scenes": [
    {
     "type": "problem",
     "title": "Code it",
     "statement": "Write dijkstra(start, roads): return the least time from start to every town. Weights are never negative.",
     "example": {
      "input": "A-B 4, A-C 1, C-B 2, B-D 1; start A",
      "output": "dist: A 0, B 3, C 1, D 4"
     },
     "note": "Needs non-negative weights.",
     "cues": {
      "example": "Same map",
      "output": "returns the least",
      "note": "No negative weights"
     },
     "say": "Now code it. A function takes a start town and the roads. Same map, start at A. It returns the least time to every town: zero, three, one, four. No negative weights."
    },
    {
     "type": "code",
     "head": "Dijkstra: set the stage",
     "say": "A road is a pair: weight, then destination. Distances start at infinity, the biggest long long. The heap holds pairs too, with greater, so the smallest distance pops first. Then set the start to zero, and push it.",
     "panels": [
      {
       "file": "sol.cpp",
       "code": "using P = pair<long long, int>;\nvector<long long> dijkstra(int s, vector<vector<P>>& g) {\n    vector<long long> d(g.size(), LLONG_MAX);\n    priority_queue<P, vector<P>, greater<P>> pq;\n    d[s] = 0;  pq.push({0, s});"
      }
     ],
     "steps": [
      {
       "lines": [
        1
       ],
       "cue": "A road is a pair"
      },
      {
       "lines": [
        3
       ],
       "cue": "start at infinity"
      },
      {
       "lines": [
        4
       ],
       "cue": "The heap holds"
      },
      {
       "lines": [
        5
       ],
       "cue": "set the start"
      }
     ],
     "notes": [
      {
       "line": 4,
       "inside": true,
       "text": "min-heap",
       "tone": "good",
       "cue": "smallest distance pops"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "code",
     "head": "Dijkstra: pop and relax",
     "say": "Pop the smallest pair. If its distance is bigger than what we know, it's stale: skip it. Otherwise relax every road. If going through here is cheaper, record it and push the new pair. A town can sit in the heap twice, and the stale check handles that. Each edge pushes at most once, and a push costs log V, so the total is O of E log V.",
     "panels": [
      {
       "file": "sol.cpp",
       "code": "    while (!pq.empty()) {\n        auto [du, u] = pq.top();  pq.pop();\n        if (du > d[u]) continue;\n        for (auto [w, v] : g[u]) {\n            if (du + w >= d[v]) continue;\n            d[v] = du + w;  pq.push({d[v], v});\n        }\n    }\n    return d;\n}"
      }
     ],
     "steps": [
      {
       "lines": [
        2
       ],
       "cue": "Pop the smallest"
      },
      {
       "lines": [
        3
       ],
       "cue": "it's stale"
      },
      {
       "lines": [
        4
       ],
       "cue": "relax every road"
      },
      {
       "lines": [
        5,
        6
       ],
       "cue": "record it"
      },
      {
       "lines": [
        6
       ],
       "cue": "push the new pair"
      },
      {
       "lines": [],
       "cue": "A town can sit"
      },
      {
       "lines": [
