    {
     "type": "code",
     "head": "Union-Find: find",
     "say": "Here's the structure. Parents live in p, sizes in s z. The constructor makes everyone their own parent, and every size one. Find: if x isn't its own parent, ask its parent for the president, and store the answer back in p of x. That one assignment is path compression.",
     "panels": [
      {
       "file": "sol.cpp",
       "code": "struct DSU {\n    vector<int> p, sz;\n    DSU(int n) : p(n), sz(n, 1) { iota(p.begin(), p.end(), 0); }\n    int find(int x) {\n        if (p[x] != x) p[x] = find(p[x]);\n        return p[x];\n    }"
      }
     ],
