    {
     "type": "code",
     "head": "Union-Find: unite by size",
     "say": "Unite finds both presidents. The same president means they're already together: return false. Otherwise hang the smaller club under the bigger one. That's union by size: it keeps every tree at most log n tall. Add the sizes, and return true.",
     "panels": [
      {
       "file": "sol.cpp",
       "code": "bool unite(int a, int b) {\n    a = find(a);  b = find(b);\n    if (a == b) return false;\n    if (sz[a] < sz[b]) swap(a, b);\n    p[b] = a;  sz[a] += sz[b];\n    return true;\n}"
      }
